# No browser verification

Do not open, drive, or screenshot a browser to verify work. The user verifies everything in the browser themselves.

- Do not use browser automation tools (navigate, click, type, snapshot, screenshot) to check pages, layout, or behavior.
- After UI or web changes, say what to check and on which routes; do not run that check yourself in a browser.
- Use non-browser checks only when they are needed to implement the change (tests, build, types, curl against an API you already started). Do not start a site "just to look at it."

```text
# ❌ BAD
Open localhost, click through Contact, screenshot the success state.

# ✅ GOOD
Contact form is wired to POST /contact.php. Please confirm submit success and error states in the browser.
```
